<title>SWEDEN: Ratos to sell German transport unit.</title>
<headline>Ratos to sell German transport unit.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish investment company Ratos AB on Wednesday said it was selling its German transport subsidiary, Fenthol &amp; Sandtmann GmbH.</p>
<p>The deal by Ratos' unit Inter Forward was in line with a company policy to streamline operations, Ratos said in a statement.</p>
<p>Fenthol &amp; Sandtmann has an annual turnover of 375 million crowns and 230 employees and is part of Inter Forward's logistics division, Ratos said.</p>
<p>No sale price was disclosed.</p>
<p>In addition, Ratos said it plans to list Inter Forward in the long term, as part of its aim to focus on core investment operations.</p>
<p>-- Birgitte Forsberg, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700 1006</p>
